    'det.dmg': "Damage", 'det.taken': "Taken", 'det.vision': "Vision", 'det.visionT': "Vision score – wards placed / destroyed / control wards bought", 'det.items': "Items", 'det.h2h': "Lane vs lane", 'det.goldAt': "Gold @{m}′", 'det.goldEnd': "Gold at the end", 'det.goldDiff': "Team gold lead (blue above, red below)", 'det.upgrading': "Older game: all details and the gold timeline are added while League runs.", 'det.towers': "Towers", 'det.inhibs': "Inhibitors", 'det.drakes': "Dragons", 'det.heralds': "Heralds", 'det.barons': "Barons",
    'help.open': "Help", 'help.helper': "## What it does\nIt shows which of your champions does best against the enemy laner – by the win rate of that matchup.\n## How to use it\n- Add the champions you play (\"+ Add champion\"). They are saved.\n- Pick your lane at the top right.\n- In champion select the enemy picks appear under \"Who are you playing against?\" – click the one you expect in your lane. Riot hides the enemies' positions in ranked, so the app guesses: the enemy who plays your lane most often (counterstats) gets a small \"?\" and is taken first – click another one if you know better.\n- Or type the enemy yourself. Your champions are listed from best to worst matchup right away.\n## Pre-load\n\"Pre-load all matchups\" fetches every opponent your pool meets on this lane – best while you queue, then champion select is instant. Kept for a day.\n## Good to know\n- The numbers come from counterstats.net (all ranks, current patch). Only champion names are sent there.\n- \"–\" means not enough games for that matchup.", 'help.tools': "## Refresh ranks\nReloads ranks, icons and levels of all accounts right away (otherwise every few minutes). League must be open.\n## Close all Riot processes\nEnds League, the Riot Client and all their helpers – the cure when something hangs or \"is already running\". The sign-in of the current account is saved first.\n## Restart League\nCloses everything and starts League again with the account you are on. Helps after a patch or when the client is stuck on a black screen.\n## Clear Riot Client cache\nDeletes the Riot Client's web cache and log files (not your sign-ins). Helps with a blank or broken client window and odd login errors.\n## Open Riot Client logs\nOpens the log folder – that's what Riot support asks for.\n## Open app data folder\nWhere Rift Switch keeps your accounts. Sign-ins and passwords there are encrypted for your Windows user only.", 'help.live': "## Lobby\nEveryone in your lobby with Solo/Duo and Flex rank.\n## Champion select\nYour team with ranks and positions. The enemy team only shows their champions (Riot hides the names until the game starts). In some queues Riot hides your team's names as well.\n## In game\nBoth teams with Solo/Duo and Flex, straight from Riot at game start. \"Multi op.gg\" opens the whole enemy team on op.gg.\n## Clash\nYour next Clash opponents as soon as the bracket is out – with ranks and a button that opens all five on op.gg.\n## Penalties & waiting times\nLeaverBuster locks, ranked suspensions, dodge timers and the low priority queue of your accounts, with the time left. Each account's own penalties are only known after logging in to it.", 'help.mh': "## Your games, all accounts\nEvery game of every saved account in one list, newest first – kept by Rift Switch itself, so it also works with League closed. There is no limit; the bin at the top deletes everything.\n## Load older games\nFetches every game the League client still has for each account on its server, plus all details of games stored without them – in one go, with progress on the button. Not during a game.\n## Filters\nAccount, queue, time (or your own dates), win/loss, champion, sorting – \"More filters\" adds kills, deaths, KDA and multikills. The summary above the list always counts what the filters show.\n## Multikills\nClick \"2× Penta Kill\" (or any other) to put those games on top.\n## Players\nBlue side left, red side right. The two small marks are Solo/Duo (filled) and Flex (outlined); a wide window writes them out. Ranks are the players' current ones – Riot doesn't keep the rank at the time of a game. Click a name to open the player on op.gg and other sites.\n## Details\nClick a game to open it: every player's stats, items and the lane against lane comparison.",
